{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1712,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You just paid nine dollars for a bucket of popcorn.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 69
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "buddy",
   "text": "Nine bucks? That's robbery. I brought my own.",
   "from": 73,
   "to": 161
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Your friend's jacket is stuffed with gas station candy. He feels like a genius.",
   "from": 165,
   "to": 271
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He paid for his ticket, so the theater still got paid, right?",
   "from": 274,
   "to": 376
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then a man in a suit walks into the box office and takes half the cash.",
   "from": 379,
   "to": 482
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That's the studio. About half of every ticket goes to whoever made the movie.",
   "from": 497,
   "to": 611
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Some deals take upwards of seventy percent.",
   "from": 615,
   "to": 662
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So the ticket barely pays for the building, the staff, or the giant screen.",
   "from": 666,
   "to": 775
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But the snack counter? The studio gets none of that.",
   "from": 778,
   "to": 850
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Out of every snack dollar, the food itself costs about seventeen cents.",
   "from": 854,
   "to": 990
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Snacks bring in only a fifth of the money, but around forty percent of the profit.",
   "from": 993,
   "to": 1112
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And after all that, the whole theater keeps about four cents per dollar.",
   "from": 1116,
   "to": 1232
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That's why theaters keep tickets low and popcorn high.",
   "from": 1235,
   "to": 1305
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Every overpriced bucket is quietly paying for your seat.",
   "from": 1309,
   "to": 1391
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Your friend didn't beat the studio. The studio already got paid.",
   "from": 1395,
   "to": 1493
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He just skipped the only part that keeps the lights on.",
   "from": 1497,
   "to": 1563
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Next week, someone new pays nine dollars for popcorn.",
   "from": 1567,
   "to": 1653
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And the lights stay on.",
   "from": 1656,
   "to": 1688
  }
 ],
